1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:24,143
I shot him before he could shoot my wife. No speech. No last question
for the sky. Nigga, I had heard everything Emperor Zero wanted to say,
and none of it mattered more than the woman standing beside my car. My
first shot struck his arm. His gun jerked sideways. Shawna fired. He
staggered against the broken bridge wall, one hand pressed to his
chest.

2
00:00:24,393 --> 00:00:44,660
For a second he stayed standing. I saw the disbelief on his face, the
terrible little hope that the world might still remember what he
called himself and correct the mistake. Then he lifted the gun again.
I fired twice. Zero fell onto the stone. The gun slipped from his
hand. He did not rise.

3
00:00:44,910 --> 00:01:09,525
I watched the man die on the bridge he had broken trying to leave
everybody else behind. Emperor Zero. All those towers. All those
guards. All those niggas told to kneel because one man could not bear
the sound of somebody walking away. Dead. My arm fell against the car
door. Shawna turned. For one second neither of us moved. Then she ran
to me.

4
00:01:09,775 --> 00:01:31,765
She caught me before I could fall out of the seat, climbed halfway
into the wrecked car, and held my face against her chest. I could hear
her heart. Fast. Alive. Mine was trying to keep up like it had finally
found a race worth winning. "Baby," I whispered. "I'm here." "You
hit?" "No." "Tell me again." "Nigga, I'm here. I'm not hit.

5
00:01:32,015 --> 00:01:54,424
Look at me." I looked. The cut near her eyebrow had stopped bleeding.
Dust streaked her face. She was crying and angry about it, which made
her look more like herself than any song, photograph, or expensive
dress ever could. "You scared the shit out of me," she said. "I had a
difficult afternoon." She laughed through the tears and hit my good
shoulder.

6
00:01:54,674 --> 00:02:17,578
"Don't be funny." "Nigga, we discussed my limited settings." She
kissed me so hard I forgot the emperor lying across the gap. Above us,
the airship lowered toward the canyon. Victor landed on the far side
first. He approached Zero carefully, moved the gun away, and looked
down at the body for a long moment. Then he looked across at me.

7
00:02:17,828 --> 00:02:43,455
He shook his head once. Finished. I closed my eyes. The word moved
through me without needing a voice. Finished. Not my life. Not the
trouble I would undoubtedly manufacture in a grocery store before the
year ended. This man. This road. This one long chain of niggas
deciding they could take what I loved and expect me to become
reasonable about it. Finished.

8
00:02:43,704 --> 00:03:05,450
Liora brought the rescue platform close enough for Shawna to help me
onto it. Victor crossed the gap and took my other side. Between them
they got me out of the Last Word while the car ticked and smoked
against the cliff. I looked back at it. The beautiful blue hood was
crumpled. One wheel pointed in a direction June had never approved.

9
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:27,388
The silver MAGNIFICENT badge still shone above the grille. "Nigga," I
whispered, "you did good." Shawna looked at the car too. "June's going
to rebuild it." "She gonna rebuild me first with a wrench." Victor
laughed and held me more firmly. "I will tell her it flew
beautifully." "Nigga, do not lead with flew." We rose into the
airship.

10
00:03:27,638 --> 00:03:51,089
Rosa reached us at the cabin door. Tank was right behind her. My
brother saw the blood on my arm, the way Victor held my weight, the
tears on Shawna's face. The nigga stopped like somebody had put a hand
through his chest. "Brother." I lifted my good hand. "Nigga, don't
start. I'm alive." He came forward and held me anyway. Carefully at
first.

11
00:03:51,338 --> 00:04:15,010
Then not carefully at all. His arms closed around me and Victor
together because apparently the nigga did not care which part of the
rescue package he hugged as long as I remained inside it. "You stupid
motherfucker," he whispered. "Accurate." "You magnificent stupid
motherfucker." "More accurate." He laughed against my shoulder. Then
the nigga cried. Not a lot.

12
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:33,017
Not a beautiful movie tear somebody could light from the side. Two
rough breaths and his face pressed into my jacket while he held the
brother he had almost lost again. I put my hand behind his head.
"Nigga, we got a wedding." He nodded without letting go.

13
00:04:33,267 --> 00:04:50,543
"Yeah." "Blue flowers." "Yeah." "You still need me to stop you dancing
like a refrigerator." He laughed, hard and sudden. Rosa wiped her
eyes. "Both of you sit down before Vega murders the survivors." The
doctor pushed through the crowd with her bag.

14
00:04:50,793 --> 00:05:14,337
"At last," she said, "somebody understands the stakes." She made me
sit on a padded bench and cut the ruined sleeve away from my arm. The
wound was ugly but shallow. The shoulder hurt worse. She checked my
hands, my eyes, the old scar, the new bruises, and every expression I
attempted to disguise as confidence. "No more lightning," she said.

15
00:05:14,587 --> 00:05:40,444
"Today?" "Aiden." "Nigga, people keep making vague medical requests."
She looked at Shawna. My wife crossed her arms. "No more lightning
until she says." I nodded. That was a prescription I understood.
Outside the airship windows, the fortress grew smaller beneath us.
Smoke rose from the courts. Cars moved through open gates. Buses
carried people toward the desert road.

16
00:05:40,694 --> 00:06:01,632
The black banners still hung, but nobody below seemed interested in
saluting them. Porsche stood by a camera mounted near the window. Her
face was wet. "I filmed it," she said. I looked up. "What part?" "The
bridge. Both of you. The whole city saw." Shawna went very still.
"They saw him die?" Porsche nodded.

17
00:06:01,882 --> 00:06:19,885
"And they saw you get Aiden out." Mercedes put a hand on Shawna's
shoulder. "Nigga, the comments are losing their minds." I laughed
weakly. "What they saying?" Shawna pointed at me without looking away
from the window. "Do not feed him while injured." Porsche ignored her.

18
00:06:20,135 --> 00:06:46,903
"One man says you are the greatest driver, officer, swordsman,
husband, and airborne passenger in recorded history." Tank sniffed and
wiped his face. "That nigga forgot singer." "Another one included
singer," Mercedes said. "Educated nigga." The cabin laughed. I leaned
back and let the sound hold me while Vega wrapped my arm. We landed in
the midnight court's outer garden. Hundreds of people waited.

19
00:06:47,153 --> 00:07:13,089
Noor stood at the front with Salma beside her. Vesper held the ledger
folio. Magnolia supported Bernard's arm. June and Adrian stood near
the Last Word's damaged transport cradle, already arguing about how to
bring the car up from the canyon. Cassius and Inez waited together,
her hand in his. Marcellus stood in the center holding the crown.
Nobody cheered immediately.

20
00:07:13,339 --> 00:07:35,218
They watched me come down the airship steps with my wife beside me, my
brother one pace behind, my arm bandaged, my coat torn, and the whole
long day still shaking in my knees. Then one of the palace workers
raised a hand. "Captain." Another voice answered. "Aiden." The names
moved through the crowd. Captain. Aiden. King.

21
00:07:35,468 --> 00:08:01,004
Nigga, I had heard people say my name because they wanted money,
protection, a photograph, a song, a fight. This sounded different. Not
purer. I was not about to become some saint because a crowd had found
a good rhythm. It sounded like people realizing the door behind them
would remain open after I left. I liked that sound. Marcellus
approached. He lifted the crown.

22
00:08:01,254 --> 00:08:20,434
"You might sit for this," he said. "Nigga, let me have posture."
Shawna laughed and steadied my elbow. The old man placed the crown on
my head. This time the crowd did not whisper. The cheering hit the
garden walls and came back twice as loud. Tank raised both fists.

23
00:08:20,684 --> 00:08:43,994
Victor shouted my name like we were back at Sky High and I had just
ruined somebody's prediction again. Cassius bowed with a hand over his
heart. Inez whistled. Knox saluted. Noor and Salma did too, followed
by guards who had spent the morning trying to decide whether I was an
enemy and were now making a different choice in front of everybody.

24
00:08:44,244 --> 00:09:05,597
Vesper stood beside me. "King of Kings," someone called. The crowd
took it up. I looked at my wife. She smiled at me, not at the crown.
That was the part that almost broke me. "You impressed?" I asked. She
moved closer. "Nigga, I'm trying to remain manageable about it." I
kissed her while the whole garden shouted.

25
00:09:05,847 --> 00:09:30,535
When the cheering softened enough for me to speak, I raised one hand.
"All right. Listen." The crowd quieted. "The emperor's dead. His roads
are open. His prisoners leave. His staff gets paid. Anybody wants to
keep shooting about it can find me after I take a fucking nap."
Laughter rolled through the garden. "The captains handle their people.
The workers decide where they work.

26
00:09:30,785 --> 00:09:54,480
The cars—" Tank sat forward. "—we're discussing the cars." The crowd
laughed harder. "And nobody," I said, looking at Bernard, "is charging
that man to rebuild his hotel." The owner covered his face. Magnolia
held him. I lowered my hand. That was enough governing for the day.
Knox approached with a palace officer carrying a velvet cushion.

27
00:09:54,730 --> 00:10:18,378
On it lay Zero's ceremonial key ring, heavy with gold. "The inner
treasury," she said. "The surviving officials are requesting your
direction." I took the keys. Nigga, some habits survive even a
meaningful afternoon. Shawna saw my expression. "Aiden." "Baby, the
wedding ain't paying for itself." She laughed and put her hand through
my arm.

28
00:10:18,628 --> 00:10:37,902
We walked into the palace together, past guards who bowed, past
workers who waved, past portraits that already looked like they
belonged to a dead man. Behind us, the airship's painted heart moved
gently in the evening wind. TANK + ROSA. Ahead of us, the treasury
doors opened.

29
00:10:38,152 --> 00:10:45,650
And for the first time in a long time, the next thing waiting on the
other side was a future we had already chosen.
